  "title": "Ukraine and Russia: US Energy Ceasefire Claim Welcomed by Zelensky, Russia Still Silent",
  "summary": "Ukraine President Volodymyr Zelensky supports a truce between Russia and Ukraine, citing the need for energy supplies, while U.S. President Donald Trump’s announcement of a ceasefire is met with initial optimism from Ukraine but not from Russia. Ukraine has been targeting Russia's oil industry for months, prompting fuel rationing and Russia's ban on diesel exports. The global crisis also came after the war on Iran curtailed oil shipments through the Strait of Hormuz.",
